          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "терять (teryát) — Old Russian терять (teryát) meant \"to destroy, to ruin\". Vasmer finds its link with the South Slavic verbs for \"to chase\" uncertain and puts the East Slavic word with тереть, \"to rub, to wear away\"."
